From 203c91306174ef99460c0d9f916e9c06e81210dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rogerbacardit <rogerbacardit@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:00:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] External knob controller on USB-A: knobs, jog, Back and
 presets

A CC from a USB-A controller was dropped. It now stands for a Move control
and is replayed through the internal router, so every page, lock and modal
treats it as the hardware:

- Schwung's convention (any channel): CC 71-78 relative, CC 102-109
  absolute -> knobs 1-8, so one controller setup serves movy and Schwung.
- A factory-default Midi Fighter Twister works with no setup: encoders
  9-16 are knobs 1-8, encoder 1 the jog (geared down) and its push the jog
  click, encoder 4's push Back, encoder 3 steps presets from any page.
  Encoder 2 (CC 1) is left alone: the engine plays it as the mod wheel.
- The Twister's rings are lit green on assigned encoders and dark on the
  rest, repainted when CCs resume after a quiet spell (it forgets on
  reconnect). USB-A MIDI out goes through a new Platform.externalSend.

Presets from any page: PresetKnob.stepAnywhere lands on the preset door,
seeds its count and index (the controller only learns them by ticking on
the door, and stepPreset refuses an empty list), steps, and returns.

Tests: logic/ext-knobs.mjs covers the mapping. Tested on a Move with a
Twister and a KeyStep Pro on a hub, on a v0.37.0 backport.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
